## Working conventions established (apply to all future sessions)
- Direct file/vim editing preferred over GUI wherever a file genuinely exists and no database-override risk applies.
- Never open Appearance → Editor → Styles panel (creates database override of theme.json).
- Be aware: editing any template via the Site Editor GUI risks creating a database "customized" copy that shadows the theme file of the same name — check with WP-CLI (`wp post list --post_type=wp_template`) if in doubt about which is authoritative.
- WP-CLI (`docker exec -it oswp-wordpress-1 wp ... --allow-root`) is the reliable tool for inspecting real state when the GUI or REST API is ambiguous or auth-restricted.
- User prefers being walked through GUI steps explicitly when GUI use is unavoidable (Site Editor navigation is not yet familiar territory).
